<region region-id="277" left="18.00" top="3822.05" width="572.00" height="43.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="3832.05" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Vectors hold the five combinations in this order: Service I, Strength I, Strength III wind 1, Strength III wind 2, Strength IV (LRFD Tables 3.4.1-1 and 3.4.1-2). TU and SH share one factor. Wind takes γWS = 1.0 where it applies; vertical wind counts only when it increases overturning.</p></text>
</region>
