<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Heading 1" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">11. Cap torsion screen (LRFD 5.7.2.1; not in the FBMP cap model)</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="534" left="18.00" top="9366.19" width="572.00" height="56.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="9376.19" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">The strap restraint is spread along the backwall and balances the overturning moment, so the torque along the cap closes to zero at both ends. Uniform torques: soil and cap self-weight over the cap length, backwall and strap over the backwall length. Point torques: bearing-level loads at the two bearings, cheek walls at the cap ends.</p></text>
</region>
